  "articleBody": "When you're dealing with interior water damage, it's easy to make a few common mistakes that can actually worsen the situation or complicate repairs. First, never enter a flooded area if there's any chance of energized outlets or submerged electrical cords. That's incredibly dangerous! Always shut off power to wet areas first if it's safe to do so. Another mistake is using a regular household vacuum to try and remove water. These aren't designed for water and can create electrical hazards or get ruined. You'll need a wet/dry vacuum or professional extraction for significant amounts of water. Ignoring wet ceiling fixtures or a sagging ceiling is also a big no-no; these are signs of serious water accumulation that could lead to a collapse. And finally, delaying professional drying when there's a lot of water is a major mistake. Basic cleanup might seem sufficient, but hidden moisture can lead to mold and structural damage. Acting quickly to get professional help for proper drying and moisture detection, like what HH Remodeling LLC offers, can prevent much bigger problems down the line and save you a lot of money and stress.",
